{"aaData": [["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-ask-for-1\" title=\"motomeru\">motomeru</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/ask-for\" title=\"ASK FOR [ask-for]\">ASK FOR [ask-for]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020719\" title=\"1-nom 2-dat 3-acc V\">1-nom 2-dat 3-acc V</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-be-a-hunter-1\" title=\"no verbal counterpart\">no verbal counterpart</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/be-a-hunter\" title=\"BE A HUNTER [be-a-hunter]\">BE A HUNTER [be-a-hunter]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/10017630793\" title=\"N/A\">N/A</a>", "Generic tense or habitual interpretation of ryoo-o siteiru &#x27;be hunting&#x27; may denote the subject&#x27;s occupation on a par with English &#x27;He hunts&#x27;."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-be-dry-1\" title=\"kawaku\">kawaku</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/be-dry\" title=\"BE DRY [be-dry]\">BE DRY [be-dry]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020747\" title=\"1-nom V\">1-nom V</a>", "Kawaku is an intransitive change-of-state verb, and Japanese does not have the adjective for &#x27;be dry&#x27;. So the stative meaning is denoted by adding the resultative auxiliary to kawaku."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-be-hungry-1\" title=\"onaka-ga suku\">onaka-ga suku</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/be-hungry\" title=\"BE HUNGRY [be-hungry]\">BE HUNGRY [be-hungry]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020747\" title=\"1-nom V\">1-nom V</a>", "No verb to denote the state of &#x27;being hungry&#x27;. Suku &#x27;become empty&#x27; is a change-of-state verb, to which the resultative aux. is added to represent the state of being hungry. The verb calls for two subjects representing the person (experiencer) and his/her stomach."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-be-sad-1\" title=\"kanasii\">kanasii</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/be-sad\" title=\"BE SAD [be-sad]\">BE SAD [be-sad]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020747\" title=\"1-nom V\">1-nom V</a>", "Kanasii is an adjective, on which the transitive verb kanasimu &#x27;(She) grieves over (his death)&#x27; is made. This verb may in turn become a causative verb kanasimaseru &#x27;(His death) makes (her) grieve&#x27;."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-beat-1\" title=\"tataku\">tataku</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/beat\" title=\"BEAT [beat]\">BEAT [beat]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020733\" title=\"1-nom (2-instr) 3-acc V\">1-nom (2-instr) 3-acc V</a>", "Tataku can express the meanings of &#x27;hit&#x27; and &#x27;beat&#x27;."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-blink-1\" title=\"mabataki-o suru\">mabataki-o suru</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/blink\" title=\"BLINK [blink]\">BLINK [blink]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020747\" title=\"1-nom V\">1-nom V</a>", "The noun mabataki &#x27;a blink&#x27; is derived from the verb mabataku &#x27;blink (one&#x27;s eyes)&#x27;, which sounds poetic or archaic in contemporary Japanese."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-boil-1\" title=\"waku\">waku</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/boil\" title=\"BOIL [boil]\">BOIL [boil]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020747\" title=\"1-nom V\">1-nom V</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-break-1\" title=\"kowasu\">kowasu</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/break\" title=\"BREAK [break]\">BREAK [break]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020733\" title=\"1-nom (2-instr) 3-acc V\">1-nom (2-instr) 3-acc V</a>", "Other transitive verbs in the semantic field of &#x27;breaking&#x27; are waru &#x27;smash, split&#x27;, kudaku &#x27;crash&#x27;, and oru &#x27;snap off&#x27;, which all have their intransitive change-of-state counterparts: wareru &#x27;smash, split&#x27;, kudakeru &#x27;crash&#x27;, and oreru &#x27;snap off&#x27;."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-bring-1\" title=\"mot-te kuru\">mot-te kuru</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/bring\" title=\"BRING [bring]\">BRING [bring]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020739\" title=\"1-nom 2-loc 3-acc V\">1-nom 2-loc 3-acc V</a>", "Mot-te kuru (lit. &#x27;come while carrying&#x27;) is a complex predicate consisting of two verbs. Japanese has no single verb that corresponds to &#x27;bring&#x27;."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-build-1\" title=\"tateru\">tateru</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/build\" title=\"BUILD [build]\">BUILD [build]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020733\" title=\"1-nom (2-instr) 3-acc V\">1-nom (2-instr) 3-acc V</a>", "The intransitive verb corresponding to the transitive verb tateru &#x27;build&#x27; is tatu &#x27;stand up, get built&#x27;, but morphologically the transitive tateru derives from the intransitive tatu and not vice versa."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-burn-1\" title=\"moeru\">moeru</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/burn\" title=\"BURN [burn]\">BURN [burn]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020747\" title=\"1-nom V\">1-nom V</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-carry-1\" title=\"hakobu\">hakobu</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/carry\" title=\"CARRY [carry]\">CARRY [carry]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020739\" title=\"1-nom 2-loc 3-acc V\">1-nom 2-loc 3-acc V</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-climb-1\" title=\"noboru\">noboru</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/climb\" title=\"CLIMB [climb]\">CLIMB [climb]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5371461865\" title=\"1-nom 2-acc V\">1-nom 2-acc V</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-cook-1\" title=\"ryoori-suru\">ryoori-suru</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/cook\" title=\"COOK [cook]\">COOK [cook]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5371461865\" title=\"1-nom 2-acc V\">1-nom 2-acc V</a>", "This is a Sino-Japanese verb. There is no native verb that corresponds to &#x27;cook&#x27;."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-cough-1\" title=\"seki-o suru\">seki-o suru</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/cough\" title=\"COUGH [cough]\">COUGH [cough]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020747\" title=\"1-nom V\">1-nom V</a>", "The noun seki &#x27;a cough&#x27; is derived from the verb seku, which is almost archaic in contemporary Japanese."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-cover-1\" title=\"kurumu\">kurumu</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/cover\" title=\"COVER [cover]\">COVER [cover]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020733\" title=\"1-nom (2-instr) 3-acc V\">1-nom (2-instr) 3-acc V</a>", "The verb kurumu means &#x27;wrap up (in a blanket/paper)&#x27;. Covering of the surface is represented by oou &#x27;cover (the surface)&#x27;, which has no intransitive counterpart."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-cut-1\" title=\"kiru\">kiru</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/cut\" title=\"CUT [cut]\">CUT [cut]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020733\" title=\"1-nom (2-instr) 3-acc V\">1-nom (2-instr) 3-acc V</a>", "Resultative adjuncts like tanzaku-ni &#x27;into rectangular slices&#x27; may be added."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-die-1\" title=\"sinu\">sinu</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/die\" title=\"DIE [die]\">DIE [die]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020747\" title=\"1-nom V\">1-nom V</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-dig-1\" title=\"horu\">horu</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/dig\" title=\"DIG [dig]\">DIG [dig]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5371461865\" title=\"1-nom 2-acc V\">1-nom 2-acc V</a>", "Horu can take a variety of objects such as &#x27;garden&#x27; (place arg.), &#x27;potatoes&#x27; (thing to be dug out), &#x27;hole, tunnel&#x27; (result of digging). The intransitive horeru means that a place becomes hollow."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-dress-1\" title=\"kiseru\">kiseru</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/dress\" title=\"DRESS [dress]\">DRESS [dress]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020719\" title=\"1-nom 2-dat 3-acc V\">1-nom 2-dat 3-acc V</a>", "The intransitive verb corresponding to the transitive verb kiseru &#x27;dress&#x27; is kiru &#x27;get dressed&#x27;, but morphologically the transitive kiseru derives from the intransitive kiru and not vice versa."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-eat-1\" title=\"taberu\">taberu</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/eat\" title=\"EAT [eat]\">EAT [eat]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5371461865\" title=\"1-nom 2-acc V\">1-nom 2-acc V</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-fear-1\" title=\"kowagaru\">kowagaru</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/fear\" title=\"FEAR [fear]\">FEAR [fear]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5371461865\" title=\"1-nom 2-acc V\">1-nom 2-acc V</a>", "The verb kowagaru &#x27;fear&#x27; is morphologically derived from the adjective kowai &#x27;be afraid&#x27;."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-feel-cold-1\" title=\"samui\">samui</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/feel-cold\" title=\"FEEL COLD [feel-cold]\">FEEL COLD [feel-cold]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020747\" title=\"1-nom V\">1-nom V</a>", "Samui is an adjective. Japanese has no stative verb meaning &#x27;be cold&#x27;."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-feel-pain-1\" title=\"itai\">itai</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/feel-pain\" title=\"FEEL PAIN [feel-pain]\">FEEL PAIN [feel-pain]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/11349361511\" title=\"1-nom 2-nom V\">1-nom 2-nom V</a>", "Itai is an adjective which takes two subjects: an experiencer and his/her body part. The intransitive verb itamu &#x27;feel pain&#x27;, derived from the adjective, can be used similarly."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-fill-1\" title=\"mitasu\">mitasu</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/fill\" title=\"FILL [fill]\">FILL [fill]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020739\" title=\"1-nom 2-loc 3-acc V\">1-nom 2-loc 3-acc V</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-follow-1\" title=\"ato-ni tuzuku\">ato-ni tuzuku</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/follow\" title=\"FOLLOW [follow]\">FOLLOW [follow]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020747\" title=\"1-nom V\">1-nom V</a>", "Ato-ni tuzuku may or may not be intentional. Its potential form can be derived if the verb takes a non-agentive subject. The intentional action of chasing is represented by ou &#x27;chase, run after&#x27;."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-frighten-1\" title=\"kowagaraseru\">kowagaraseru</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/frighten\" title=\"FRIGHTEN [frighten]\">FRIGHTEN [frighten]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5371461865\" title=\"1-nom 2-acc V\">1-nom 2-acc V</a>", "The verb kowagaraseru is the causative of kowagaru &#x27;fear&#x27; in item 12. Both predicates take two core arguments syntactically, but their realization patterns are different. Semantically, the causative kowagaraseru can select the causer of emotion/agent, experiencer, and the target of emotion, the non-causative kowagaru, experiencer and target of emotion."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-give-1\" title=\"ataeru\">ataeru</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/give\" title=\"GIVE [give]\">GIVE [give]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020719\" title=\"1-nom 2-dat 3-acc V\">1-nom 2-dat 3-acc V</a>", "Japanese distinguishes several verbs of giving (as well as receiving) in terms of the person and social status of giver and recepient. Of these, ataeru is the most neutral verb."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-go-1\" title=\"iku\">iku</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/go\" title=\"GO [go]\">GO [go]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020751\" title=\"1-nom 2-loc V\">1-nom 2-loc V</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-grind-1\" title=\"hiku\">hiku</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/grind\" title=\"GRIND [grind]\">GRIND [grind]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5371461865\" title=\"1-nom 2-acc V\">1-nom 2-acc V</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-hear-1\" title=\"kiku\">kiku</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/hear\" title=\"HEAR [hear]\">HEAR [hear]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5371461865\" title=\"1-nom 2-acc V\">1-nom 2-acc V</a>", "Kiku can express an agentive as well as a spontaneous meaning of &#x27;hearing&#x27;. Another verb kikoeru can be seen as a potential form of kiku, and expresses a spontaneous meaning, having the case frame of &quot;dative-nominative&quot;. Kiku must take an accusative argument referring to some kind of sound (e.g. voice) and cannot take a person as an accusative argument, unlike English. Thus, anata-o kiku (you-acc hear) is not a possible form in Japanese."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-help-1\" title=\"tetudau\">tetudau</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/help\" title=\"HELP [help]\">HELP [help]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5371461865\" title=\"1-nom 2-acc V\">1-nom 2-acc V</a>", "In many cases, tetudau &#x27;assist, give a helping hand&#x27; may be substituted for by the verb tasukeru &#x27;support, aid, help&#x27;. The latter verb has another meaning of &#x27;save someone&#x27;s life&#x27;."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-hide-1\" title=\"kakusu\">kakusu</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/hide\" title=\"HIDE [hide]\">HIDE [hide]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5371461865\" title=\"1-nom 2-acc V\">1-nom 2-acc V</a>", "There is an intransitive verb kakureru &#x27;hide oneself&#x27; that is morphologically related to the transitive kakusu &#x27;hide&#x27;. It will not be good to relate them by valency change, because the intransitive verb selects the subjects which have potential to move by themselves. Presumably, these two verbs are best treated as independent lexical items, despite their morphological affinity."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-hit-1\" title=\"tataku\">tataku</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/hit\" title=\"HIT [hit]\">HIT [hit]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020733\" title=\"1-nom (2-instr) 3-acc V\">1-nom (2-instr) 3-acc V</a>", "Tataku can express the meanings of &#x27;hit&#x27; and &#x27;beat&#x27;."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-hug-1\" title=\"dakisimeru\">dakisimeru</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/hug\" title=\"HUG [hug]\">HUG [hug]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5371461865\" title=\"1-nom 2-acc V\">1-nom 2-acc V</a>", "The verb dakisimeru is a compound verb consisting of daku &#x27;hold in one&#x27;s arms&#x27; and simeru &#x27;wring, tighten&#x27;."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-jump-1\" title=\"tobiagaru\">tobiagaru</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/jump\" title=\"JUMP [jump]\">JUMP [jump]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020747\" title=\"1-nom V\">1-nom V</a>", "Tobiagaru is a compound verb consisting of tobu &#x27;jump&#x27; and agaru &#x27;go up&#x27;. The single verb tobu &#x27;jump&#x27; can be used alone in the construction."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-kill-1\" title=\"korosu\">korosu</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/kill\" title=\"KILL [kill]\">KILL [kill]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020733\" title=\"1-nom (2-instr) 3-acc V\">1-nom (2-instr) 3-acc V</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-know-1\" title=\"siru\">siru</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/know\" title=\"KNOW [know]\">KNOW [know]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5371461865\" title=\"1-nom 2-acc V\">1-nom 2-acc V</a>", "Japanese has no stative verb for &#x27;know&#x27;. Siru is a change-of-state verb meaning &#x27;get to know&#x27;, and the resultative aux. is added to represent the stative meaning."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-laugh-1\" title=\"warau\">warau</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/laugh\" title=\"LAUGH [laugh]\">LAUGH [laugh]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020747\" title=\"1-nom V\">1-nom V</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-leave-1\" title=\"saru\">saru</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/leave\" title=\"LEAVE [leave]\">LEAVE [leave]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5371461865\" title=\"1-nom 2-acc V\">1-nom 2-acc V</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-like-1\" title=\"ki-ni-iru\">ki-ni-iru</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/like\" title=\"LIKE [like]\">LIKE [like]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5371461865\" title=\"1-nom 2-acc V\">1-nom 2-acc V</a>", "Ki-ni-iru has a complex form in its origin, but is now lexicalized into a single predicate. It can take three different case marking patterns of &quot;nominative-accusative&quot; (cf. ex. 14), &quot;dative-nominative&quot; (cf. ex. 102), and &quot;nominative-nominative&quot; (cf. ex. 103)."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-live-1\" title=\"sumu\">sumu</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/live\" title=\"LIVE [live]\">LIVE [live]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020751\" title=\"1-nom 2-loc V\">1-nom 2-loc V</a>", "Sumu is not a stative verb but an activity verb, so the progressive is necessary to denote the present state."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-load-1\" title=\"tumu\">tumu</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/load\" title=\"LOAD [load]\">LOAD [load]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020739\" title=\"1-nom 2-loc 3-acc V\">1-nom 2-loc 3-acc V</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-look-at-1\" title=\"miru\">miru</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/look-at\" title=\"LOOK AT [look-at]\">LOOK AT [look-at]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5371461865\" title=\"1-nom 2-acc V\">1-nom 2-acc V</a>", "Miru expresses an agentive meaning of &#x27;looking&#x27;, but can also be used to express the spontaneous meaning of &#x27;coming into sight&#x27;."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-meet-1\" title=\"au\">au</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/meet\" title=\"MEET [meet]\">MEET [meet]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/7081416451\" title=\"1-nom 2-dat V\">1-nom 2-dat V</a>", "Unlike the English &#x27;meet&#x27;, the verb au cannot take an accusative object."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-name-1\" title=\"yobu\">yobu</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/name\" title=\"NAME [name]\">NAME [name]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020729\" title=\"1-nom 2-acc 3-quot V\">1-nom 2-acc 3-quot V</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-peel-1\" title=\"muku\">muku</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/peel\" title=\"PEEL [peel]\">PEEL [peel]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5371461865\" title=\"1-nom 2-acc V\">1-nom 2-acc V</a>", "Syntactically, the &#x27;skin/peel&#x27; argument and its possessor are represented by a single NP in modification relation, rather than by separate constituents."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-play-1\" title=\"asobu\">asobu</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/play\" title=\"PLAY [play]\">PLAY [play]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020747\" title=\"1-nom V\">1-nom V</a>", "With this verb, &#x27;toy&#x27; is marked with instrumental marker. Since this verb does not have a transitive counterpart, it is not taken to participate in argument increasing alternation."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-pour-1\" title=\"sosogu\">sosogu</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/pour\" title=\"POUR [pour]\">POUR [pour]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020739\" title=\"1-nom 2-loc 3-acc V\">1-nom 2-loc 3-acc V</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-push-1\" title=\"osu\">osu</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/push\" title=\"PUSH [push]\">PUSH [push]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5371461865\" title=\"1-nom 2-acc V\">1-nom 2-acc V</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-put-1\" title=\"oku\">oku</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/put\" title=\"PUT [put]\">PUT [put]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020739\" title=\"1-nom 2-loc 3-acc V\">1-nom 2-loc 3-acc V</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-rain-1\" title=\"huru\">huru</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/rain\" title=\"RAIN [rain]\">RAIN [rain]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020747\" title=\"1-nom V\">1-nom V</a>", "The verb huru takes as subject something that falls from the sky, e.g. rain, snow, hail, and ash emitted from a volcano."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-roll-1\" title=\"korogaru\">korogaru</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/roll\" title=\"ROLL [roll]\">ROLL [roll]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020747\" title=\"1-nom V\">1-nom V</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-run-1\" title=\"hasiru\">hasiru</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/run\" title=\"RUN [run]\">RUN [run]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020747\" title=\"1-nom V\">1-nom V</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-say-1\" title=\"yuu\">yuu</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/say\" title=\"SAY [say]\">SAY [say]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/12333943651\" title=\"1-nom 2-dat UTT3 V\">1-nom 2-dat UTT3 V</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-scream-1\" title=\"sakebi-goe-o ageru\">sakebi-goe-o ageru</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/scream\" title=\"SCREAM [scream]\">SCREAM [scream]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020747\" title=\"1-nom V\">1-nom V</a>", "Sakebu &#x27;shout, cry, scream&#x27; is also possible."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-search-for-1\" title=\"sagasu\">sagasu</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/search-for\" title=\"SEARCH FOR [search-for]\">SEARCH FOR [search-for]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5371461865\" title=\"1-nom 2-acc V\">1-nom 2-acc V</a>", "The direct object of the verb sagasu corresponds to the &#x27;for&#x27;-argument of English &#x27;search&#x27;. The place argument of &#x27;search&#x27; (&#x27;search the place&#x27;) is represented by the accusative marker designating the traversal path of motion, as in yama-o noboru &#x27;climb the mountain&#x27;."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-see-1\" title=\"mieru\">mieru</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/see\" title=\"SEE [see]\">SEE [see]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/7081256030\" title=\"1-dat 2-nom V\">1-dat 2-nom V</a>", "Mieru takes the stative case pattern of &quot;dative-nominative&quot;, but cannot take the case pattern of &quot;nominative-accusative&quot;."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-send-1\" title=\"okuru\">okuru</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/send\" title=\"SEND [send]\">SEND [send]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020739\" title=\"1-nom 2-loc 3-acc V\">1-nom 2-loc 3-acc V</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-shave-a-body-part_person-1\" title=\"soru\">soru</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/shave-a-body-part_person\" title=\"SHAVE (a body part/person) [shave-a-body-part_person]\">SHAVE (a body part/person) [shave-a-body-part_person]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5371461865\" title=\"1-nom 2-acc V\">1-nom 2-acc V</a>", "Like muku &#x27;peel&#x27;, the verb soru can take both the &#x27;beard/hair&#x27; argument and its possessor argument designating the place where the &#x27;hair/beard&#x27; grows."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-shout-at-1\" title=\"sakebu\">sakebu</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/shout-at\" title=\"SHOUT AT [shout-at]\">SHOUT AT [shout-at]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020719\" title=\"1-nom 2-dat 3-acc V\">1-nom 2-dat 3-acc V</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-show-1\" title=\"miseru\">miseru</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/show\" title=\"SHOW [show]\">SHOW [show]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020719\" title=\"1-nom 2-dat 3-acc V\">1-nom 2-dat 3-acc V</a>", "The ditransitive verb miseru is formed by adding a lexical transitivizing affix -se to the transitive stem mi- &#x27;see&#x27;."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-sing-1\" title=\"utau\">utau</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/sing\" title=\"SING [sing]\">SING [sing]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5371461865\" title=\"1-nom 2-acc V\">1-nom 2-acc V</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-sink-1\" title=\"sizumu\">sizumu</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/sink\" title=\"SINK [sink]\">SINK [sink]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020747\" title=\"1-nom V\">1-nom V</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-sit-down-1\" title=\"kosi-o orosu\">kosi-o orosu</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/sit-down\" title=\"SIT DOWN [sit-down]\">SIT DOWN [sit-down]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020751\" title=\"1-nom 2-loc V\">1-nom 2-loc V</a>", "The verb suwaru is also possible in this construction."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-sit-1\" title=\"suwaru\">suwaru</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/sit\" title=\"SIT [sit]\">SIT [sit]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020751\" title=\"1-nom 2-loc V\">1-nom 2-loc V</a>", "Unlike English &#x27;sit&#x27;, Japanese suwaru does not have a stative meaning."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-smell-1\" title=\"nioi-o kagu\">nioi-o kagu</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/smell\" title=\"SMELL [smell]\">SMELL [smell]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020747\" title=\"1-nom V\">1-nom V</a>", "Nioi-o kagu &#x27;take a smell of&#x27; is an intentional action, whereas nioi-ga suru &#x27;perceive the smell of&#x27; is non-intentional."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-steal-1\" title=\"nusumu\">nusumu</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/steal\" title=\"STEAL [steal]\">STEAL [steal]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5371446322\" title=\"1-nom 2-abl 3-acc V\">1-nom 2-abl 3-acc V</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-take-1\" title=\"toru\">toru</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/take\" title=\"TAKE [take]\">TAKE [take]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5371446322\" title=\"1-nom 2-abl 3-acc V\">1-nom 2-abl 3-acc V</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-talk-1\" title=\"hanasu\">hanasu</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/talk\" title=\"TALK [talk]\">TALK [talk]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020719\" title=\"1-nom 2-dat 3-acc V\">1-nom 2-dat 3-acc V</a>", "dative argument is optional"], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-teach-1\" title=\"osieru\">osieru</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/teach\" title=\"TEACH [teach]\">TEACH [teach]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020719\" title=\"1-nom 2-dat 3-acc V\">1-nom 2-dat 3-acc V</a>", "Osieru can have either a theme or a recipient as an object. When the object is a theme, it takes a &quot;nominative-dative-accusative&quot; case frame, and when the object is a recipient, it takes a &quot;nominative-accusative&quot; case frame (cf. ex 101)."], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-tear-1\" title=\"yaburu\">yaburu</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/tear\" title=\"TEAR [tear]\">TEAR [tear]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5371461865\" title=\"1-nom 2-acc V\">1-nom 2-acc V</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-tell-1\" title=\"tugeru\">tugeru</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/tell\" title=\"TELL [tell]\">TELL [tell]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020719\" title=\"1-nom 2-dat 3-acc V\">1-nom 2-dat 3-acc V</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-think-1\" title=\"kangaeru\">kangaeru</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/think\" title=\"THINK [think]\">THINK [think]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5371461865\" title=\"1-nom 2-acc V\">1-nom 2-acc V</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-throw-1\" title=\"nageru\">nageru</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/throw\" title=\"THROW [throw]\">THROW [throw]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020739\" title=\"1-nom 2-loc 3-acc V\">1-nom 2-loc 3-acc V</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-tie-1\" title=\"tunagu\">tunagu</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/tie\" title=\"TIE [tie]\">TIE [tie]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/6536020741\" title=\"1-nom (2-instr) 3-loc 4-acc V\">1-nom (2-instr) 3-loc 4-acc V</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-touch-1\" title=\"sawaru\">sawaru</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/touch\" title=\"TOUCH [touch]\">TOUCH [touch]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5371461865\" title=\"1-nom 2-acc V\">1-nom 2-acc V</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-wash-1\" title=\"arau\">arau</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/wash\" title=\"WASH [wash]\">WASH [wash]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5371461865\" title=\"1-nom 2-acc V\">1-nom 2-acc V</a>", ""], ["<a class=\"Value\" href=\"https://valpal.info/values/nucl1643-wipe-1\" title=\"hukitoru\">hukitoru</a>", "<a class=\"Parameter\" href=\"https://valpal.info/parameters/wipe\" title=\"WIPE [wipe]\">WIPE [wipe]</a>", "<a class=\"CodingFrame\" href=\"https://valpal.info/codingframes/5371461865\" title=\"1-nom 2-acc V\">1-nom 2-acc V</a>", "Hukitoru is a compound verb consisting of huku &#x27;wipe&#x27; and toru &#x27;remove&#x27;. This verb takes the theme, but not the locative, as its object. Thus, teeburu-o hukitoru &#x27;wipe the table&#x27; is not possible. Huku can be used as an independent verb; in this case, the verb can take either the theme or the locative as its object, as in teeburu-o huku &#x27;wipe the table&#x27; and doro-o huku, lit. &#x27;wipe the dirt&#x27;, the latter of which is not possible with English wipe."]], "sEcho": "1", "iTotalRecords": 80, "iTotalDisplayRecords": 80}